1. Definitions

"Licensor" means the copyright holder(s) who own and license the
applicable FabCAD original code.

"Licensed Code" means the original source code, object code, scripts,
tests, and accompanying technical documentation in the FabCAD repository
to the extent they are owned or validly licensable by the Licensor. It
does not include Third-Party Materials or User Content.

"Third-Party Materials" means software, libraries, fonts, assets, or
other materials distributed with or used by FabCAD that are owned by
others and subject to their own license terms.

"User Content" means models, project files, drawings, sketches,
manufacturing data, and other designs created or imported by a FabCAD
user.

"Internal Use" means using, reproducing, running, modifying, or deploying
Licensed Code inside an individual or organization's own operations,
including commercial business operations, evaluation, proof-of-concept,
research, production, and internal network services used by its personnel
or contractors acting on its behalf. Internal Use does not include
distributing Licensed Code as part of a product to external recipients
or operating a Commercial Hosted Service for third parties.

"Hosted Service" means operating Licensed Code so that persons other
than the operator's personnel or contractors acting on its behalf can
use its functionality over a network. Internal Use and access to the
Official FabCAD Service as an end user are not Hosted Services.

"Noncommercial Free Hosted Service" means a Hosted Service that is free
of charge to all users and is operated without direct or indirect
commercial exploitation of the Licensed Code or the service. This
excludes charging for access, usage, or required support; paid tiers;
advertising or sponsorship revenue; promotion of paid products or
services; sale of user data; and commercial lead generation. An
operator's unrelated business activities alone do not disqualify an
otherwise genuinely noncommercial, free Hosted Service.

"Commercial Hosted Service" means a Hosted Service that does not meet
all the conditions for a Noncommercial Free Hosted Service.

"Commercial Product Distribution" means selling, licensing, or
distributing Licensed Code as part of a product, application, device,
or software offering to external recipients for direct or indirect
commercial benefit. Selling physical products created using FabCAD,
or selling User Content and its outputs, is not Commercial Product
Distribution.

"Official FabCAD Service" means the FabCAD application deployed by or
with the express authorization of the Licensor, including the official
web application identified by the project at
https://fooping-tech.github.io/FabCAD/app/.

